/**
 * DYNAMIC TASK GRAPH — the durable shape of "what this task is, right now".
 *
 * A todo list answers "what is next" and nothing else. This layer needs two more: WHICH PHASE is this (a
 * `testing` phase and a `coding` phase call for different knowledge, and the phase belongs to the NODE),
 * and WHAT DID WE LEARN HERE (a node points at knowledge via `knowledgePointers`, and the knowledge
 * records which nodes used it, written by `recordKnowledgeRefs`).
 *
 * TWO INVARIANTS. `start` is fixed: exactly one, always present, never removed — a graph without it is a
 * different task, not an edited one. The goal can be LOCKED, because a stated objective must not be
 * quietly rewritten by the same model working on it (that is how "fix the crash" becomes "delete the
 * crashing test"). The lock covers the DESTINATION, not the journey — see `graph-goal-lock.ts`.
 *
 * STORAGE. One JSON document, `<memoryDir>/task-graph.json`, written atomically under a lease; the audit
 * trail is one `history` entry per accepted mutation.
 */

